wer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268621}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afbfa683-c522-59c8-966d-dac5ae4cf63a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75007" :question/problem "Find $|r(2)|$ given that $r(t)=⟨t+1,\\,\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨2+1,\\,\\sqrt{2+1},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(2)| & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+3+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
